# Botpress ADK (backend)

- **Runtime**: Prefer **Node.js v22+** (matches ADK docs). Keep `engines.node` in `package.json` honest.
- **ADK vs this repo**: This folder is a **standalone HTTP API** that can later call Botpress (ADK client, webhooks, or cloud APIs). Do not assume the ADK CLI layout unless we add an `adk`-style subfolder; keep route handlers thin and push agent logic into dedicated modules when integrations land.
- **TypeScript**: Strict mode, ESM (`"type": "module"`, NodeNext resolution). Use shared response types in `src/types/api.ts` and keep JSON schemas on routes aligned with those types.
- **Flow**: User journey is **questionnaire → search → results**. The questionnaire route is a stub until persistence and scoring exist; search should accept parameters that will eventually come from the questionnaire (e.g. `questionnaireSessionId` or future filter query params).
- **Secrets**: Botpress tokens and workspace IDs via environment variables only; never commit credentials.
- **Docs**: https://botpress.com/docs/for-developers/adk/introduction and ADK repo https://github.com/botpress/adk
